{
  "id": "dsa-3143",
  "title": "Html tag in HTML - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>HTML is a language full of diverse elements, and one such element is the&nbsp;</span><code><span>&lt;html&gt;</span></code><span>&nbsp;tag. This tag, standing for ‘HyperText Markup Language’, is used to define the root of an HTML or XHTML document.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>It serves as the main container for all other HTML elements, excluding the&nbsp;</span><code><span>&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</span></code><span>&nbsp;declaration</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>It follows the&nbsp;</span><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-3768\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</span></code><span>&nbsp;declaration</span></a><span> and requires both opening and closing tags.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"syntax\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Syntax</span></h3><pre><span>&lt;html&gt; HTML Contents... &lt;/html&gt;</span></pre><h3 id=\"html-document-structure\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>HTML Document Structure</span></h3><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"html-structure\" height=\"675\" src=\"./images/dsa-3143-img-1.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250423175128033405/html-structure.png 806w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250423175128033405/html-structure-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250423175128033405/html-structure-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250423175128033405/html-structure-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250423175128033405/html-structure-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250423175128033405/html-structure-768.png 768w\" width=\"806\"><figcaption>HTML Structure</figcaption></figure><h2 id=\"default-css-settings\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Default CSS Settings</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The following default values are mostly displayed by the current browsers:</span></p><pre><span>html&nbsp;{</span><br><span>&nbsp; display:&nbsp;block;</span><br><span>  visibility: visible</span><br><span>}</span></pre><h3 id=\"attribute-value\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Attribute Value</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><code><span>&lt;html&gt;</span></code><span> tag includes the </span><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-3769\" rel=\"noopener\"><code><span>xmlns</span></code></a><span> attribute. This attribute defines the namespace for attributes, ensuring proper interpretation and compatibility of XHTML elements.</span></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Note: </strong></b><span>The &lt;html&gt; tag supports the </span><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-3770\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Global Attributes</span></a><span> in HTML.</span></p></blockquote><h2 id=\"html-html-tag-examples\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>HTML Tag Examples</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example 1:</strong></b><span>&nbsp; This example illustrates the &lt;html&gt;  tag element in HTML.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">&lt;!-- html tag starts here --&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>GeeksforGeeks<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">h2</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n        html Tag\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">h2</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">&lt;!-- html tag ends here --&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example 2:</strong></b><span> In this example, we will be using the </span><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-3769\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>xmlns attribute</span></a><span> inside the &lt;html&gt;  tag.&nbsp;</span></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">    PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" </span>\n<span class=\"cp\">\"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\"&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span> <span class=\"na\">xmlns</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"https://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml/\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">head</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">title</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>html Tag<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">title</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">style</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"k\">color</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">green</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"k\">text-align</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">center</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">style</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">head</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>GeeksforGeeks<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">h2</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n        html Tag\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">h2</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs></div>",
  "textContent": "HTML is a language full of diverse elements, and one such element is the <html> tag. This tag, standing for ‘HyperText Markup Language’, is used to define the root of an HTML or XHTML document.It serves as the main container for all other HTML elements, excluding the <!DOCTYPE> declarationIt follows the <!DOCTYPE> declaration and requires both opening and closing tags.Syntax<html> HTML Contents... </html>HTML Document StructureHTML StructureDefault CSS SettingsThe following default values are mostly displayed by the current browsers:html {  display: block;  visibility: visible}Attribute ValueThe <html> tag includes the xmlns attribute. This attribute defines the namespace for attributes, ensuring proper interpretation and compatibility of XHTML elements.Note: The <html> tag supports the Global Attributes in HTML.HTML Tag ExamplesExample 1:  This example illustrates the <html>  tag element in HTML.\n            HTML\n\n    <!DOCTYPE html>\n<!-- html tag starts here -->\n<html>\n<body>\n    <h1>GeeksforGeeks</h1>\n    <h2>\n        html Tag\n    </h2>\n</body>\n</html>\n<!-- html tag ends here -->\n\nExample 2: In this example, we will be using the xmlns attribute inside the <html>  tag. \n            HTML\n\n    <!DOCTYPE html\n    PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" \n\"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\">\n<html xmlns=\"https://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml/\">\n\n<head>\n    <title>html Tag</title>\n    <style>\n        h1 {\n            color: green;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            text-align: center;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n\n<body>\n    <h1>GeeksforGeeks</h1>\n    <h2>\n        html Tag\n    </h2>\n</body>\n\n</html>",
  "url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/html/html-html-tag"
}
